lements) updated immediately after each field edit with no save or refresh action performed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Section reorder (Education moved above Experience) and visibility toggle (Skills hidden/shown) were both reflected immediately in the preview panel without save/refresh, and the new layout persisted while switching templates and tabs within the session.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After editing and returning to dashboard, the resume card showed 'Updated Aug 26, 2026' (today) and appeared first under Newest First sort. Reopening the resume showed all edits retained automatically with no explicit save action taken.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Added 8 experience entries with long descriptions plus existing summary/education/skills. All 8 experience items, with full untruncated description text, rendered in preview.experience.list. The preview document grew to 3729px height (exceeding the ~720px viewport), and the page became scrollable (html scrollHeight 3794 vs clientHeight 720), allowing the complete resume to be viewed via scrolling; no content was clipped or hidden.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Navigated between editor tabs, back to dashboard, and reopened the resume. Contact (Jane Doe, email, phone, location), summary, custom section headings, both experience entries, education entry, and skill (JavaScript) all remained exactly as entered.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After duplicating, editing the copy's contact name/summary did not change the original (verified original still showed 'Jane Doe' and original summary). Then edited the original's contact name to 'Jane Doe-Original'